{
  "norad": 60237,
  "name": "GRBBeta",
  "callsign": "HA2GRB",
  "modulation": "GFSK9k6",
  "ax25_pid": "0xF0",
  "reference": "https://gitlab.com/librespacefoundation/satnogs/satnogs-decoders/-/blob/master/ksy/grbbeta.ksy",
  "document": "SatNOGS decoders \"grbbeta.ksy\" (Kaitai Struct); https://grbbeta.tuke.sk/. The U (UHF) and V (VHF) beacons have the same 14-field layout as LASARsat's. The PSU frame offsets are the field order of psu_hk_t in grbbeta.ksy (little-endian).",
  "note": "Only the ASCII U/V radio beacons, the free-text/digipeated messages, the CW beacon and the binary PSU housekeeping frame (CSP header: source 2, source port 9; 75 bytes) are defined, from grbbeta.ksy. The PSU frame and the CW beacon have not been checked against a received frame; the PSU values are raw (the ksy gives volts/amperes/watts as u2 without a scale) and the byte offset assumes the payload handed to the decoder starts at the CSP header.",
